          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Is that high?",
          "answer": "I need a bit more detail before I can answer. Which reading or result do you mean? For example:\n\n- Blood pressure\n- Blood glucose (sugar)\n- Cholesterol\n- A lab value, such as HbA1c\n\nPlease also share the number and its unit (for example mmol/L, mg/dL, or mmol/mol). If you mean the HbA1c of 58 from your earlier message, tell me the unit that your lab report uses.\n\nOnce I have the value, I can explain how it compares with commonly used reference ranges from the sources I have. The answer also depends on personal factors, such as your age, other health conditions, and medicines, so your clinician is the right person to interpret it for you.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
